{
  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "a1b2c3d4-hop1-alon-g00000000001",
    "name": "HopAlong — Backend API",
    "description": "📮 Complete Postman collection for the **HopAlong backend** (Express + MongoDB + Socket.IO).\n\nCovers **every route** mounted in `backend/server.js`:\n\n| Folder | Prefix | Routes |\n|---|---|---|\n| 🏥 Health | `/health`, `/api/health` | 3 |\n| 🔐 Auth | `/api/auth` | 5 |\n| 👤 Users | `/api/users` | 5 |\n| 🧳 Trips | `/api/trips` | 7 |\n| 🤝 Join Requests | `/api/requests` | 6 |\n| 💬 Messages | `/api/messages` | 3 |\n\n### 🚀 How to use\n1. Start the backend: `cd backend && npm run dev` (default `http://localhost:5000`).\n2. (Optional) Seed demo data: `cd backend && npm run seed` — 6 demo users + 10 trips.\n3. Run **Auth → Login User** first. The test script auto-saves `token` and `userId`.\n4. Run **Trips → Create Trip** to auto-save `tripId`, **Requests → Send Join Request** to save `requestId`, **Messages → Send Message** to save `messageId`.\n5. Or run the entire collection with the **Collection Runner** in order.\n\n### 🔑 Demo credentials (after `npm run seed`)\n| Email | Password |\n|---|---|\n| `rahul.sharma@iitr.ac.in` | `password123` |\n| `priya.patel@iitr.ac.in` | `password123` |\n| `arjun.kumar@iitr.ac.in` | `password123` |\n\n### ⚠️ Notes\n- Registration only accepts `*.iitr.ac.in` emails.\n- Rate limit: **100 requests / 10 min** per IP on `/api/*`.\n- Trip `startDate` must be today or in the future; `endDate` must be after `startDate`.\n- Approve/Reject/Update/Delete trip routes require the **organizer's** token.\n- Real-time events (chat, notifications) run over Socket.IO and are not covered by REST requests.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "auth": {
    "type": "bearer",
    "bearer": [
      { "key": "token", "value": "{{token}}", "type": "string" }
    ]
  },
  "variable": [
    { "key": "baseUrl", "value": "http://localhost:5000" },
    { "key": "token", "value": "" },
    { "key": "userId", "value": "" },
    { "key": "tripId", "value": "" },
    { "key": "requestId", "value": "" },
    { "key": "messageId", "value": "" }
  ],
  "item": [
